title: Referendum to Recall President DuFour
subtitle: The results have come in.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: impeachment_ref_week == week and impeachment_ref_month == month and impeachment_ref_year == year
on-arrival: {!
Q.dufour_ref_votes = 0;

Q.dufour_ref_votes += Q.marcher_votes;
Q.dufour_ref_votes += Q.collectivist_votes;
if (Q.sapd_formed) Q.dufour_ref_votes += Q.sapd_votes;

if (Q.impeachment_ddp) Q.dufour_ref_votes += Q.ddp_votes;
if (Q.impeachment_gold) Q.dufour_ref_votes += Q.gold_votes;
if (Q.impeachment_lvp) Q.dufour_ref_votes += Q.lvp_votes;
if (Q.impeachment_unionist) Q.dufour_ref_votes += Q.unionist_votes - Q.bvp_votes;
if (Q.impeachment_bvp) Q.dufour_ref_votes += Q.bvp_votes;
Q.dufour_ref_votes += Q.royalist_gallax_votes;
if (Q.nvf_exist) Q.dufour_ref_votes += Q.nvf_votes;

Q.dufour_ref_votes -= (100 - Q.pro_republic) / 5;

Q.dufour_ref_votes = parseFloat(Q.dufour_ref_votes.toFixed(1));
!}
max-visits: 1

= Referendum to Recall President DuFour

After a month of intense, violence-filled campaigning and relentless propaganda from both sides, the Commonwealth people now vote on DuFour’s fate—a decision that may determine the future of the Republic itself.

Unlike previous referendums, this one requires only a majority of those voting—not of all eligible voters—to succeed.

- @results: The nation votes...

@results
go-to: hindenburg_ref_win if dufour_ref_votes >= 50; hindenburg_ref_lose if dufour_ref_votes < 50


@hindenburg_ref_win
on-arrival: {!
Q.dufour_gone = 1;

Q.rubicon_president_week = Q.week + 4;
Q.rubicon_president_month = Q.month;
Q.rubicon_president_year = Q.year;
Q.rubicon_president_time = Q.rubicon_time + 4;

let added_months = Math.floor(Q.rubicon_president_week / 4);
Q.rubicon_president_month += added_months;
Q.rubicon_president_week = Q.rubicon_president_week % 4;
if (Q.rubicon_president_week === 0) Q.rubicon_president_week = 1;

if (Q.rubicon_president_month > 12) {
    Q.rubicon_president_month -= 12;
    Q.rubicon_president_year += 1;
}

Q.president = "Burnell (acting)";
if (Q.judicial_reform >= 4) Q.president = "Großmann (acting)"

Q.pro_republic += 10;
Q.commons_kvp -= 4; 
Q.disfavored_kvp -= 4;
Q.burgher_kvp -= 2;

if (Q.aspd_other) {
    Q.commons_other -= 4; 
    Q.disfavored_other -= 4;
    Q.burgher_other -= 2;
}
!}

The referendum succeeds with [+ dufour_ref_votes +]% of the vote—the Commonwealth is saved! If the current coalition holds, we may finally elect a democratic president capable of guiding the nation out of the chaos left by DuFour and Staal.

Disgraced and isolated, DuFour is forced to resign from the presidency. In his place, [? if president == "Burnell (acting)": Erwin Burnell?][? if president == "Großmann (acting)": Hermann Großmann?], President of the Commonwealth Court, has been elevated to acting president until new elections are held.

Presidential elections are scheduled for Week [+ rubicon_president_week +] of [+ rubicon_president_month : month +], [+ rubicon_president_year +].

@hindenburg_ref_lose

Unfortunately, the referendum has failed with [+ dufour_ref_votes +]% of the vote. So much for nothing.

DuFour has been agitated by the weakness of the incumbent government and, under the influence of his Camarilla, will decide on Trevannon's successor himself, as he considers another set of Assembly elections unacceptable.

- @schizo

@schizo
title: Crown Prince Wilhelm...?
on-arrival: {!
Q.chancellor = "Hohenzollern";
Q.vice_chancellor = "Goodryke";

const contentElement = document.getElementById('content');
contentElement.style.backgroundColor = '#312115';
contentElement.style.color = '#FFFFFF';

const toolsWrapper = document.getElementById('tools_wrapper');
if (toolsWrapper) {
  toolsWrapper.style.display = 'none';
}

const header = document.querySelector('header');
header.style.color = '#ffffff';
!}

Under the influence of Franz von Goodryke—and apparently Staal as well—DuFour has appointed Prince Halvard, a scion of the old imperial line, as Chancellor, reportedly with his father’s blessing.

It is clear the chaos of the past year has taken its toll. In the end, DuFour now trusts no one but his dearest friend, Goodryke. It's unknown of the former chancellor's reasoning behind such a pick, but perhaps he would've hoped that reinstating a monarchy, the people can rally around him as they once rallied around DuFour. 

A bloody three-way civil war is inevitable.

- @papen_civil_war